Z||000000||ArchMagi||10-11-2000||12:56 AM||||Im just curious here...<P>Iv herd alot of talk about the Iron Duke and Tech 4 putting out 92HP and of 134lbs/torque.<P>But iv herd nothing of the 6cyl stats... anyone?<P>Weight, how much difference is from the Notchback/Fastback? or engine sizes?<P>Thanks in advance.||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FST2M6||10-11-2000||08:43 AM||||GT Bastards 86 SE V6 4spd (w/lots of mods) (before and after headers) not worth the money on a 2.8.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6headerdyno_4.jpg">  <P><BR>BlackGTs dyno before and after the K&N filter.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BlackGTdyno_1.jpg">  <P>these numbers are at the wheels!<BR><p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 10-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||10-11-2000||10:40 AM||||Weight:<BR>Coupe 4cyl = 2464<BR>85 Coupe V6 = 2505 <BR>86/87 SE 4cyl = 2531<BR>85 GT 86/87 SE V6 = 2572<BR>86/87 GT = 2696<BR>(I don't have stats on 88's)<P>Horsepower and torque:<BR>84 to 86 4cyl = 92hp 134 torque<BR>85/86 V6 = 140hp 170 torque<BR>87 4cyl = 98hp 135 torque<BR>87 V-6 = 135hp 165 torque<P>These figures were taken from the book "Fiero" by Gary Witzenburg<BR>There is a newer version of the book that covers 88's but I don't have a copy....Yet.<P><BR>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 10-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||count_iblis||10-11-2000||10:51 AM||||so the 86 gt v6 has 5 mor horse power and 5 more on the torque?  so is that the year to get for horsepower and torque?||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||10-11-2000||11:30 AM||||not really... as you can see.. BlackGTs car has only 22k on it's new motor while mine had 96k and with little mods, k&n, 2.5" exhaust, MSD and dyno tuning and headers.. oh sorry.. Jeffs car now.. has more Hp than Todds. with way less miles. by nearly 20hp and 10lbft AT THE WHEELS.. both of these cars are 86s with 4spd run at the same temerature just minutes apart. proper tuning on the SE brought his recent motor GT with the same gearing down. and would SMOKE him at will at a light...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||10-11-2000||01:50 PM||||The differences in hp/torque were just because of different testing methods needed to get around some new emmision/noise law in 87.  Still the same engine.  About the only v6 you don't want would be a very early 85, because they have smaller crankshaft main bearing journals than the rest of the years.<P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 151,000 miles and counting!         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">      <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||88formula||10-11-2000||08:47 PM||||My 88 Formula weighs 2700 pounds and it is a notchback. The difference between the GT and notchback fiero is 50 pounds.||||reg||1
